---
// Política de Cookies (em inglês, o idioma do site). Cookies de análise (Google Analytics) só com consentimento, pelo
// aviso de cookies (src/components/AvisoCookies.astro). O site não tem cookies necessários: não há formulário nem
// Turnstile. Se entrar mapa, vídeo incorporado ou parecido, atualizar este texto e o aviso.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { autor } from '../data/autor';
---

<Legal
  title={`Cookie Policy — ${autor.nome}`}
  description={`Which cookies the website of ${autor.nome} uses, what they are for, and how to accept, decline or control them in your browser.`}
  titulo="Cookie Policy"
  href="/cookie-policy/"
  atualizado="2026-11-21"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what cookies are, which ones this site uses and how you can control them. It complements the
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files that a website stores in your browser to remember information from one page to the next.
  </p>

  <h2>Which cookies this site uses</h2>
  <p>
    The site <strong>uses no advertising cookies</strong> and builds no browsing profiles. Fonts, scripts and images
    are served from this site itself, not from third parties. The only cookies are these:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics: Google Analytics, only if you accept.</strong> With your consent, Google Analytics stores the
      cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> (for up to 2 years) to count visits and show which pages are
      viewed most, where visitors come from and how they move through the site. The data is used in aggregate. It is
      processed by Google, under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your choice in the cookie notice is also kept in your browser (in <code>localStorage</code>, not in a cookie), so
    that the question is not asked again on every page.
  </p>

  <h2>How to accept or decline</h2>
  <p>
    On your first visit, a notice asks whether you accept analytics cookies. Google Analytics is only loaded after you
    click <strong>Accept</strong>. To change your choice at any time, use
    <button type="button" class="link-button" data-preferencias-cookies>Cookie preferences</button>
    (the same link is in the footer of every page). When you decline, the Google Analytics cookies are deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Links to papers, DOIs, GitHub, YouTube, Google Scholar, Google Patents, Lattes and other sites take you away from
    this one. From there on, the privacy and cookie policies of each of those services apply.
  </p>

  <h2>How to control cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can view, block or delete cookies in your browser settings (Chrome, Safari, Firefox, Edge and others). The
    site works the same with all cookies blocked.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If other kinds of cookies come into use, this page and the cookie notice will be updated, and your consent will be
    asked before they are activated. The date of the last update is always at the top of the page.
  </p>
</Legal>
